# G5/G5.1 vectors aimed at places where breakage is expected: state that
# outlives a block, modes the spline path forgets, degenerate geometry and
# float rounding on an axis that must not move. Numbers in [] are catalog IDs
# from ../../README.md.

# ---- laser mode [43] --------------------------------------------------------

# Control: the bench sees the laser power that G1 and G0 pass to the planner.
= [43] laser mode: G1 burns at S, G0 does not
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set laser 1
F1000
M3 S1000
G1 X1 Y0
power 1000
G0 X2 Y0
power 0

# Laser mode lets only G1/G2/G3 burn (gcode.c "If in laser mode"), so a
# spline is cut with the power of a rapid.
= [43] laser mode: G5 burns at S like G1 @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set laser 1
F1000
M3 S1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
power 1000

= [43] laser mode: G5.1 burns at S with M4 @bug
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set laser 1
F1000
M4 S1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5
power 1000

# ---- units, offsets, distance mode [44] -------------------------------------

# The implicit I/J of a continuation are kept in mm: switching to G20 must
# not scale them again. Same direction either way, so only the model catches it.
= [44] implicit I/J across G21 -> G20 stay in mm
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
set smooth 1
G21 G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G20 G5 X0.78740157 Y0 P0 Q-0.19685039
pos -80 -100 -10

# G54 + G92 + G20 + G90 at once: the second curve is the first one shifted.
= [44] G54, G92 and G20 stacked: same segments as the plain curve
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
G92 X7 Y-3
G20 G5 X-0.11811024 Y-0.11811024 I-0.11811024 J0.11811024 P0.11811024 Q0.11811024 F39.370079
same -10 0 0
pos -120 -100 -10

# ---- degenerate geometry [45] -----------------------------------------------

# Start == end, both handles on one ray: the tool runs out to 0.75 of the
# handle and straight back. The chord of the whole curve has zero length and
# every probe window around the tip has coinciding ends.
= [45] spike: cubic out and back reaches the tip and stops there
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 I8 J6 P8 Q6
travel X 12
travel Y 9
junction 50
pos -100 -100 -10

= [45] spike: quadratic out and back reaches the tip and stops there
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X0 Y0 I8 J6
travel X 8
travel Y 6
junction 50
pos -100 -100 -10

# ---- float rounding on a fixed or monotone axis [46] ------------------------

# X is constant along the whole curve and sits exactly on a rounding boundary
# (1 step/mm, X-100.5). The lerp (1-t)*a + t*a is not exactly a in float
# unless the compiler reassociates it (-ffast-math does); any 1-ulp wobble
# rounds to the other step and X moves back and forth.
= [46] fixed X on a half-step boundary never steps
set steps 1
G53 G0 X-100.5
F1000
G5 Y-90 I0 J3 P0 Q-3
travel X 0
travel Y 10

# ulp(60000) = 0.004 mm = one step at 250 steps/mm: rounding of the walker
# must not turn a monotone X into a reversal, nor the bump in Y into a wobble.
= [46] far from origin: monotone X and a single bump in Y
F1000
G53 G0 X-60000 Y-60000
G5 X-60010 Y-60000 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
travel X 10
travel Y 4.5

# ---- what keeps and what ends a G5 series [47] ------------------------------

# LinuxCNC keeps -P/-Q of the last G5 whatever comes between (convert_spline
# reads cycle_i/cycle_j); grbl keys on the motion mode, which non-modal
# commands and rejected lines leave alone.
= [47] series survives G4, a rejected G1, G28 and G92
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G28.1
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G4 P0.1
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5
G1 X30 Y0 Q1 -> error
G5 X30 Y0 P0 Q5
G28
G5 X10 Y0 P0 Q5
G92 X0 Y0
G5 X10 Y0 P0 Q5
pos -80 -100 -10

= [47] soft reset ends the series
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
reset
F1000
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5 -> error

= [47] check mode: the series continues without motion
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
set check 1
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5
X30 Y0 P0 Q5
pos -70 -100 -10

# P/Q with no axis word in G5 mode: no motion, so the words are unused; they
# must not become the implicit I/J of the next curve either.
= [47] P/Q alone in G5 mode are unused and not stored
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J5 P0 Q5
P0 Q9 -> error:36
G5 X20 Y0 P0 Q5
pos -80 -100 -10

# ---- words [48] -------------------------------------------------------------

# LinuxCNC rejects G4 with G2/G3 "because they both use P" and forgot G5;
# grbl gives P to the dwell first and the curve misses it. Either way the
# line must not run: neither a dwell nor a curve with a dwell time as handle.
= [48] G4 and G5 on one line both want P: rejected
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G4 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error:28
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G4 P0.5 X20 Y0 Q3 -> error:28
pos -90 -100 -10

= [48] G5.1 continuation needs I/J on every block and takes no P/Q
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5
X20 Y0 I5 J-5
X30 Y0 -> error:28
X30 Y0 I5 J5 P1 -> error:36
X30 Y0 I5 J5 Q1 -> error:36
pos -80 -100 -10

= [48] repeated Q, zero inverse-time feed
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 Q4 -> error:25
G93 G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F0 -> error:22
pos -100 -100 -10
